SUMMARY:[FREE] Meet the Maker-in-Residence Josie Everett (AKA Rosie Josie)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260818T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260818T193000
DTSTAMP:20260802T095750Z
UID:cbd8a0da13a52204c8a1c19a512c52aa@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,reading
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nThe Summer 2026 Maker-in-Residence\, J
 osie Campbell (AKA Rosie Josie) is a Chicago based printmaker. To create h
 er prints\, she hand carves original art into a linoleum tile using fine w
 oodcarving tools\, ink the carved tile\, and press the paper into it by ha
 nd using a spoon. When she removes the paper from the block the reverse pr
 int of the linoleum tile is revealed. This means each one of the prints is
  made by hand and slightly different. Inspiration for her art is drawn fro
 m folklore\, mythology\,\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.c
 om/events/6a4e9ff77d04302f00167bbf
LOCATION:Sulzer Regional\, 4455 N. Lincoln Ave.\, Chicago\, IL 60625
URL:https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/events/6a4e9ff77d04302f00167bbf
